16. What is full load and incremental load?

full load -> means we have to load the entire data from a tables. so we will truncate the table and load it
incremental load -> copy only the newly updated datas

17. How will you identify whether a table is suitable for full load or incremental load?

check the table size, if smaller the face is good usecase
if table size is big, then incremental load is good usecase.
doesnot have a any column to identify the updating records then full load
otherwise its incremental.


18. What are the rules for incremental load?

load type should be incremental
need modified date for filtering
watermark column for indentifying the source table filtering column name
watermark value contains last modified date, so that if new record come, we can filter with watermark value.
deltakey is used for identify a record.

19. How will you achieve incremental load?
with watermark column, we can get the column name of source table which the modified date will be stored.
with watermark value, we will have the last modified date.
so if date is watermark column, then  watermark column > watermark value -> it will filter the records which are previously stored and only new record will be retrieve.


